    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a limited slate today, with several core offensive pillars currently sidelined due to team off-days. Consequently, the focus shifts to **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber**, who represent our strongest offensive engine against Scott. **Trea Turner** leads the way with a 66.39 efficiency score; his placement at the top of the order provides a 10% lift, and his elite speed profile remains our primary hedge in the scarce SB category. **Kyle Schwarber** follows closely with a 63.04 score, benefiting from an xwOBA of .377 and a favorable park factor, though he must contend with a dynamic platoon disadvantage against the right-handed Scott. **Carson Benge** rounds out the active roster with a 54.68 score. While his matchup against Nola is statistically challenging given the opposing starter's 3.87 xERA, **Carson Benge** earns a marginal start thanks to a +7% platoon edge, effectively keeping him ahead of the inactive bench depth.\n\nThe bench situation is largely dictated by scheduling gaps, as **Yordan Alvarez**, **Junior Caminero**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Christian Yelich** are all unavailable today. Among the fringe roster options like **Caleb Durbin**, **Hyeseong Kim**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Colt Keith**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Luke Raley**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez**, none could force their way into the lineup due to the lack of active games. The primary risk today remains the volatility of the matchup against Nola; if **Carson Benge** struggles early against Nola\u2019s command, we have limited flexibility to pivot given the current bench vacancies. We will monitor the official lineup cards for any late-breaking wind shifts in the stadium that could impact the home run potential for both **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber**.",
